That happened because we decided

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.490
to take a risk and be different.

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:14.219
So how can you be
different in your category,

00:11:14.219 --> 00:11:16.415
in your career, in your field of interest.

00:11:16.415 --> 00:11:19.014
Whatever you're doing, how
can you purposely choose

00:11:19.014 --> 00:11:21.591
to evolve and do something
different cuz that's a risk

00:11:21.591 --> 00:11:25.808
and sure, not all risks are
rewarded, but I'll tell you

00:11:25.808 --> 00:11:28.165
what's never rewarded, stagnation.

00:11:28.165 --> 00:11:30.422
- I think risk is important
for everything company,

00:11:30.422 --> 00:11:33.210
I think it is the essence
of entrepreneurship

00:11:33.210 --> 00:11:35.185
whether you're the smallest
company in the world

00:11:35.185 --> 00:11:37.631
or like Google, the second
largest company in the world

00:11:37.631 --> 00:11:40.381
to take smart risks all the time.

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:44.151
I run this experiment
frequently with groups

00:11:44.151 --> 00:11:47.401
where I give them two choices,
choice A and choice B.

00:11:47.401 --> 00:11:50.380
So choice A is you get
to deliver $1,000,000

00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:54.680
of bottom line value to your
company this year guaranteed.

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:58.358
Choice B, you get to
deliver $1,000,000,000

00:11:58.358 --> 00:12:00.443
of bottom line value to
your company this year

00:12:00.443 --> 00:12:02.464
but only with one chance in 100.

00:12:02.464 --> 00:12:04.307
So everyone does the mental math, I say

00:12:04.307 --> 00:12:05.375
"Who wants choice A?"

00:12:05.375 --> 00:12:06.661
Nobody raises their hand.

00:12:06.661 --> 00:12:08.221
"Who wants choice B?"

00:12:08.221 --> 00:12:10.468
Everybody raises their hand,
it's got an expected utility,

00:12:10.468 --> 00:12:12.765
it's 10 times higher than choice A.

00:12:12.765 --> 00:12:15.192
And then I say, "Who here
believes that your boss

00:12:15.192 --> 00:12:17.309
"wants you to choose choice B?"

00:12:17.309 --> 00:12:20.018
And not a single person in
the room raises their hand.

00:12:20.018 --> 00:12:22.611
I mean, it's typically
a large multinationals

00:12:22.611 --> 00:12:25.087
who want to be innovative.

00:12:25.087 --> 00:12:27.825
And then I say, "You don't
need a lecture on innovation,

00:12:27.825 --> 00:12:30.715
"you need a new boss,
you need a new context."

00:12:30.715 --> 00:12:32.992
I really think it's the
context that matters.

00:12:32.992 --> 00:12:36.752
We all inherently understand
that taking smart risks

00:12:36.752 --> 00:12:38.386
is the right thing to do.

00:12:38.386 --> 00:12:40.767
Now what counts as smart
and what counts as a risk

00:12:40.767 --> 00:12:43.106
is different in different
parts of a company

00:12:43.106 --> 00:12:45.675
or companies of different sizes.

00:12:45.675 --> 00:12:49.997
You can tolerate a PR fiasco much easier

00:12:49.997 --> 00:12:52.644
if you're a tiny company
cuz no one's watching you

00:12:52.644 --> 00:12:54.477
than if you're a large
company for example.

00:12:54.477 --> 00:12:56.682
So the calculus is
different but the principle

00:12:56.682 --> 00:12:57.818
is still the same.

00:12:57.818 --> 00:13:00.406
The only way to stay
sharp, to stay growing,

00:13:00.406 --> 00:13:04.043
to stay relevant is to take
smart risks all the time.

00:13:04.043 --> 00:13:05.642
- [Narrator] When we talk of

00:13:05.642 --> 00:13:07.364
(slow piano music)

00:13:07.364 --> 00:13:10.447
risks, we are being confronted

00:13:11.920 --> 00:13:13.920
every single day

00:13:15.478 --> 00:13:18.061
with choices we have to make

00:13:19.666 --> 00:13:22.867
that are going to change our life forever.

00:13:22.867 --> 00:13:26.052
(slow piano music)

00:13:26.052 --> 00:13:30.631
Those that believe in
the power of their dreams

00:13:30.631 --> 00:13:32.798
end up manifesting them.

00:13:38.846 --> 00:13:42.207
Being brave, taking risks,

00:13:42.207 --> 00:13:44.399
following your heart.

00:13:44.399 --> 00:13:47.816
A lot of us are comfortable with our life

00:13:49.008 --> 00:13:51.425
but through that comfort

00:13:54.044 --> 00:13:55.961
comes a lot of anxiety,

00:13:56.905 --> 00:14:00.730
a lot of worry, a lot of stress.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:02.249
Why?

00:14:02.249 --> 00:14:06.332
Because we are still living
the same old routine.

00:14:09.394 --> 00:14:12.983
Risks are all about expansion,

00:14:12.983 --> 00:14:15.066
embracing the new.

00:14:16.067 --> 00:14:19.487
So you have to get uncomfortable

00:14:19.487 --> 00:14:21.570
to feel at peace.

00:14:27.070 --> 00:14:29.487
Risks are

00:14:31.989 --> 00:14:34.475
all about uncertainty.

00:14:34.475 --> 00:14:37.233
That's why a lot of us,

00:14:37.233 --> 00:14:40.400
we stay away from it,

00:14:41.604 --> 00:14:43.547
well away from it.

00:14:43.547 --> 00:14:44.964
But you see,

00:14:46.943 --> 00:14:50.360
we are not afraid of the unknown.

00:14:52.144 --> 00:14:56.607
Our projections of the unknown

00:14:56.607 --> 00:14:59.190
is what is terrifying.

00:15:02.664 --> 00:15:06.581
Just imagine, picture the scenario.

00:15:07.577 --> 00:15:11.052
You have 24 hours to live,

00:15:11.052 --> 00:15:12.885
what are you going to do?

00:15:13.777 --> 00:15:16.189
(ponderous piano music)

00:15:16.189 --> 00:15:17.022
(swoosh)

